Z||000000||Lewis||02-25-2000||10:25 PM||||I can not start my car.  My car would not start hot. After it cooled down then it would start.  Someone mentioned that I change the selinoid so I did that today.  Now the car will not start at all.  I had it on a hoist and jumped the terminals on the starter and it started right up so I am assuming that it is not a starter problem. I hear no noise from the starter at all.  I have lights and so forth.  Someone mentioned a module but I am not sure where or what module this may be.  I had to run wires from the starter to a switch inside the car in order to start it other wise i would not have been able to get it home.  Also I can not get in my trunk.  The lock to the trunk broke but the electric switch did work until now..i am not sure if this means anything but i can not get to the engine compartment.  Is there any way to bypass this switch or jump it so I can work on the car..i thought this may have something to do with my problem some kind of relay or something that is connected to the ignition.  I am baffled and need some advice.  Any thing anyone can do to help would greatly be appreciated.  The car is a 1985 gt with automatic trans...thanks...||||reg||9
Z||000001||Luperman||02-25-2000||11:06 PM||||have you checked your fuse for the trunk release it also supplys power for your courtesy light in the passenger compartment so if your interior light does'nt work then your fuse is more than likely blown.<BR>As for your starting problem ,on the automatics they have a switch called a neutral safety switch which does not allow a car to start unless it is in park or neutral sometimes these switchs go bad, you can try starting the car in neutral or go to the switch uplug it and jumper the wires it is located on the trans mission itself .hope this helps good luck. Donald||||reg||6
Z||000002||DRH||02-27-2000||03:42 AM||||The Trunk Release only works in Park or Neutral. It has a relay that grounds thru the P/N switch and the solenoid. The release won't work if there is a problem with the P/N switch or the wiring to the starter. You can bypass the relay. It is located under the dash on the right side of the steering column. It has 3 wires going to it (Yellow, Gray/Black, Black/White). Unplug it and jumper Gray/Black to Black/White. The Trunk Release switch should work now. If not, you can remove the jumper and run 12V directly to the black/White wire. This will bypass everything except the release solenoid and the wire running to it.<P>For the REAL problem... double check the purple wire going to the starter solenoid, it should be going to the "S" terminal. Check the P/N switch Luperman mentioned. It is on top of the tranny. Unplug and jumper the yellow wire to the purple wire to test.<P>Good luck, David.<BR>||||reg||1
